{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations are met.\n\n- **Trait implementation.** The `language!` invocation for `PlainText` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs` is marked `{impl}`. It expands to `impl super::OutlineLang for PlainText`. That impl provides `name`, `extensions`, `outline`, `fingerprint_scheme` and `search_structure`, and the scheme is `\"plain-text-structural-v1\"`.\n- **Default and cheap clone.** The macro declares `PlainText` as a unit struct deriving `Clone, Copy, Debug, Default`. Cloning therefore copies nothing and rebuilds no configuration, and the type has a `Default` value.\n- **No claimed extensions.** `extensions()` returns `PROFILE.extensions`. In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` that field is `&[]`, so the language claims no extensions.\n- **Filename fallback.** `OutlineContent::parse_source` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs` first calls `languages::registry().for_path(filename)`. If that returns nothing, it calls `Self::parse_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`.\n  - `Registry::for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/language.rs` returns `None` when the path has no extension (`path.extension()?`). It also returns `None` when no provider claims the lowercased extension.\n  - Filenames without an extension, and filenames whose extension is unclaimed, therefore get `PlainText`. The extension match is case-insensitive.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/profile.rs#fn[profile_for_path]` falls back to `plain::PROFILE` in the same way.\n\nThe text delegates the one-child-per-nonblank-line outline shape to `requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults` and the plain-text item requirements, so I did not assess it here. Tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs` also exercise the extension-less default (`bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline` and `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors`). I found no gaps, and there are no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "d364693a64f673cea5b31c5d57cc4436a3d085824fd398288e275ce0c804733a",
